-- title:
--   Partial Atkin–Lehner involution commutes with the ℓ-degeneracy map
-- statement:
--   Let $N_0,q,\ell$ be natural numbers with $N_0$ and $\ell$ nonzero and $q$ prime, and assume $q\nmid N_0\ell$. Here, for a nonzero level $N$, $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,N$ is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$) generated by the series $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,(jq)$ for the nonzero divisors $d\mid N$, where $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d$ is the ring homomorphism of Laurent series multiplying all exponents by $d$ (substitution $q\mapsto q^{d}$), and $\mathrm{atkinLehnerInvolutionFull}\,N\,\ell$ is a chosen $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(N\ell)$ interchanging the generators attached to $d$ and to $d\ell$ for every nonzero $d\mid N$ (the identity automorphism if no such $\sigma$ exists). Given $f$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(N_0q)$ and $f'$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}(N_0\ell q)$ whose underlying Laurent series satisfy $f'=\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\ell\,(f)$, the conclusion is the equality of Laurent series $$\mathrm{atkinLehnerInvolutionFull}\,(N_0\ell)\,q\,(f')=\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\ell\bigl(\mathrm{atkinLehnerInvolutionFull}\,N_0\,q\,(f)\bigr).$$
--
--   This is the $w_q$-equivariance of the degeneracy map $f\mapsto f(q^{\ell})$ between the function fields of level $N_0q$ and level $N_0\ell q$, for a prime $q$ prime to $N_0\ell$: the partial Atkin–Lehner involution at $q$ commutes with raising the uniformiser to the $\ell$-th power. It is used in the compatibility of the $w$-morphisms in the pinned degeneracy data, via [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.w_hom_comp_eq_comp_w_hom_of_pinned`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.w_hom_comp_eq_comp_w_hom_of_pinned).
